## Natural Diamonds: What "Close to 2.5ct" Actually Means

Natural asscher inventory at 2.5ct does not exist in certified form. This is not a shortage. It is a structural supply pattern.

The closest certified naturals available right now are:

**GIA 2.31ct E-VVS2 at [$31,990](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/16991410?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — This is the largest certified natural asscher below 2.5ct in current inventory. E color is one step from colorless. VVS2 means inclusions are invisible to the naked eye and extremely difficult to find even at 10x.

At 2.31ct, the face-up size is approximately 7.4mm — visually close to 2.5ct. The GIA certificate provides full traceability for origin, cut, color, and clarity. This is a stone you can wear for thirty years and pass down with complete confidence in its provenance.

**GIA 3.26ct F-VVS2 at [$36,991](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28507345?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — If you want to be clearly above 2.5ct in natural, the next certified option jumps to 3.26ct. F color is excellent. VVS2 clarity is above the floor.

At 3.26ct the face-up is approximately 8.1mm — noticeably larger than 2.5ct. This stone is for buyers who decide to step up to the 3ct tier after finding nothing at 2.5ct. The $5,001 premium over the 2.31ct buys almost a full carat more of natural rarity.

